      "body": "### Project URL\n\nhttps://github.com/Archerkattri/progressbeam\n\n### Category\n\nJS\n\n### Project Title\n\nSlim accessible progress bar for browsers, NProgress done right\n\n### Project Description\n\nNProgress (26k stars) is effectively unmaintained, and it was never accessible. ProgressBeam is an independent continuation of that thin-top-bar idea: real progressbar semantics with labeled status, reduced-motion support, explicit fail/cancel/pause states, lifecycle events, plus zero-dependency adapters for fetch, routers, React, Next.js and Vue. It ships ESM, CommonJS and TypeScript declarations, enforces size budgets in CI, and is verified with Playwright across Chromium, Firefox and WebKit. Fits any web app showing navigation or request progress, and doubles as a study in accessible component design.\n\n### Highlights\n\nAccessibility-first where NProgress has none (real role, status announcements), a dependency-free core with optional adapters, and size budgets plus cross-browser tests guarding every release.\n\n### Example Code\n\n```js\nimport ProgressBeam from 'progressbeam'\nimport 'progressbeam/progressbeam.css'\n\nProgressBeam.start()\n// load a route or request\nProgressBeam.done()\n```\n\n### Screenshots or Demo Videos\n\nhttps://raw.githubusercontent.com/Archerkattri/progressbeam/master/docs/output-demo.gif",
